  {
    "id": "989f3e0c7e845b1f6e798172",
    "path": "parquet::file::properties::BloomFilterPropertiesBuilder::with_max_ndv",
    "name": "with_max_ndv",
    "owner": "parquet::file::properties::BloomFilterPropertiesBuilder",
    "crate": "parquet",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn with_max_ndv(self, ndv: u64) -> Self",
    "docs": "Sets the maximum expected number of distinct values used to size the\nbloom filter before folding.\n\nWhen unset, the default is `1_048_576` (see [`DEFAULT_BLOOM_FILTER_NDV`]),\nwhich at the default fpp of 5% reserves roughly 1 MiB per column for the\nfilter bitset, derived as follows:\n\n```text\nndv = 1,048,576, fpp = 0.05\n  0.05^(1/8)                         ≈ 0.6877\n  1 - 0.6877                         ≈ 0.3123\n  ln(0.3123)                         ≈ -1.164\n  num_bits = -8 * 1,048,576 / -1.164 ≈ 7,206,000 bits\n                                     ≈   900,750 bytes (~900 KB)\n  next_power_of_two(900 KB)          = 1 MiB (= 1,048,576 bytes)\n```",
